-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/714e5e7b-0208-55c4-a521-134b76052d0a
-- title:
--   Igusa smooth-point data over all constant layers, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and all function fields are intermediate fields of the Laurent series field over the relevant base. Here $q$ is a prime with $q=3$ (hypothesis `hq3`), $M'\ge 1$ is an integer with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. The fields involved are: $\mathcal{F}_0=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field; $\mathcal{F}=$ `fieldBar q M'`, which is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with $H=$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of the unit-group reduction `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`; and over $\kappa$ the fields `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` $=\kappa(j,j_{M'})$, generated by the reductions `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of the $q$-expansions of $j$ and $j(M'\tau)$, and `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`. A `Place K F` is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$, and a principal ideal ring; `ord` is minus the logarithm of its adic valuation, `IsRational` means that $K$ surjects onto its residue field, and `evalAt f` is the element of $K$ representing the residue of $f$ when $f$ is integral at the place and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   The hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   *Supersingular places.* $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$, and `hW` says that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' κ`: the rational places $w$ which are affine geometric points (`IsAffineGeomPlace`) with $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the generator `jGeomGen κ M'` lying in the supersingular $j$-set `ssJSet q κ`.
--
--   *Constant reduction.* `hle` is the inclusion $\mathcal{F}_0\le\mathcal{F}$. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathcal{F}_0$ to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\mathcal{F}_0$ with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A\to\kappa$ on constants, together with a scaling clause making every non-zero element have non-zero residue after multiplication by a constant, and a map on places compatible with degrees and with divisors of functions. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that $R_0$ computes coefficientwise reduction: whenever a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ has coefficientwise image in $\mathcal{F}_0$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *Igusa rings.* $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, the set of primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` denotes the automorphism of $\mathcal{F}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ characterised by `IsLevelAutBar` (its effect on quotients of $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ is that of $\gamma$ under the embedding sending $\zeta'$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$), the identity when no such automorphism exists. $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ assigns a valuation subring of $\mathcal{F}$ to each point of [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), the projective line over $\mathbb{Z}/q$. The hypothesis `hIg_inf` describes $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at `lineInfty q` $=[1:0]$: $f$ belongs to it precisely when there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having non-zero coefficientwise reduction and $f\cdot y=x$ after coefficientwise inclusion into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$. `hIg` says that every point $\ell$ of the projective line is $\mathrm{red}_q(\gamma)\cdot[1:0]$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\ell$ the preimage of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{[1:0]}$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` says $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; `hIg_perm` says that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the family $(O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\ell)_\ell$ is permuted by taking preimages under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ`.
--
--   *Supersingular rings.* $O^{\mathrm{ss}}$ assigns a valuation subring of $\mathcal{F}$ to each $s\in W$. `hSS_A` says a constant from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ exactly when it lies in $A$. `hSS_over` says that for $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which is integral at every place of $\mathcal{F}_0$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which the coefficientwise image of `jq` is integral, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathcal{F}$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference between the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$. `hSS_fix` says each $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ is its own preimage under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t\in O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ such that $t-a$ is a unit of $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ for every $a\in A$.
--
--   *Regular prolongation.* $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\mathcal{F}$ to `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, i.e. a valuation subring with surjective residue map of kernel the maximal ideal, inducing $A\to\kappa$ on constants and satisfying the same scaling clause; `hR` identifies $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{[1:0]}$, and `hR₀O` says that $f\in\mathcal{F}_0$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when its image in $\mathcal{F}$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{[1:0]}$.
--
--   *Ramification element.* $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$.
--
--   *Small constants.* $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lies in $A$; the ring $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); `hκ` says every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$; `hstab` says every $\tau\in\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ preserving $A$ maps $k_0$ into $k_0$.
--
--   *Auxiliary prime and tame element.* $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   *Layers of constants.* $\iota$ is a type, $K:\iota\to$ intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with each $K_n$ finite over $k_0$, and $A_n$ is a valuation subring of $K_n$ with $x\in A_n$ iff $x\in A$ (`hAn`).
--
--   With $\mathcal{F}$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to\mathcal{F}$, the conclusion asserts the existence of an intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathcal{F}/k_0$, a finite set $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over $\kappa$, subrings $S_{Q,n}\subseteq\mathcal{F}$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_{Q,n}:A_n[X]\to S_{Q,n}$ and $\chi_{Q,n}:S_{Q,n}\to\kappa$, and sets $D_{Q,n}$ of places of $\mathcal{F}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, indexed by places $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` and by $n\in\iota$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   (1) The $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $F_0$ is all of $\mathcal{F}$. (2) $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. (3) $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ and $W$ have the same cardinality. (4) There is a ring homomorphism $j:$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` $\to$ `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` such that, for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, the image of $f$ in $\mathcal{F}$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue is $j$ of its $R_0$-residue; and $Q\in N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ holds precisely when there is $s\in W$ with $g$ integral at $s$ iff $j(g)$ is integral at $Q$, for all $g$. (5) Every valuation subring of $\mathcal{F}$ which contains all constants from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and is not all of $\mathcal{F}$ is a principal ideal ring.
--
--   (6) For every place $Q\notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ the following hold. First, for every $n\in\iota$: (a) the residue map $A_n\to\kappa$ is surjective; (b) the constants from $A_n$ lie in $S_{Q,n}$; (c) $\varphi_{Q,n}$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; (d) $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a)$ is the constant image of $a$ in $\mathcal{F}$; (e) $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$; (f) $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(X))=0$; (g) for every $c\in A_n$ with residue $0$ there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi:S_{Q,n}\to A_n$ which is a section of $\varphi_{Q,n}\circ C$, reduces to $\chi_{Q,n}$ on residues, and sends $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ to $c$; (h) every $f\in S_{Q,n}$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue is integral at $Q$, and the residue at $Q$ of that element is the image of $\chi_{Q,n}(f)$ under $\kappa\to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; (i) $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue has $Q$-order $1$; (j) $D_{Q,n}$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ at which every $f\in S_{Q,n}$ is integral with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and for which $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ precisely when $\chi_{Q,n}(f)=0$; (k) $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)\ne\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,c)$ for every $c\in A_n$; (l) $S_{Q,n}$ is local with maximal ideal the kernel of $\chi_{Q,n}$; (m) $S_{Q,n}$ is Noetherian and a unique factorisation monoid; (n) $S_{Q,n}$ is contained in $E_n:=$ the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_n$ in $\mathcal{F}$ together with $F_0$, and every element of $E_n$ is a quotient of two elements of $S_{Q,n}$ with non-zero denominator; (o) if $c_1,\dots,c_m\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ are linearly independent over $K_n$ and $a_1,\dots,a_m\in E_n$ satisfy $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ in $\mathcal{F}$, then all $a_i=0$; (p) there is a generator $\varpi$ of the maximal ideal of $A_n$, non-zero, such that $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi)$ is prime in $S_{Q,n}$, an element $f\in E_n$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ precisely when it is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in S_{Q,n}$ and $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi)\nmid h$, and for every prime $p$ of $S_{Q,n}$ not associated to $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x\in S_{Q,n}$ there is a monic polynomial over $A_n$ whose image under $\varphi_{Q,n}\circ C$, evaluated at $x$, is divisible by $p$; (q) for every ring homomorphism $\chi:S_{Q,n}\to A_n$ sectioning $\varphi_{Q,n}\circ C$ and reducing to $\chi_{Q,n}$, the kernel of $\chi$ is generated by $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)-\varphi_{Q,n}(C(\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(X))))$; (r) there is a finite subset $G\subseteq S_{Q,n}$ such that every $f\in S_{Q,n}$ can be written $f\cdot h=g$ with $g,h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the constants from $A_n$ and $h$ the image of a unit of $S_{Q,n}$. Secondly, the family $(S_{Q,n})_n$ is monotone: $K_n\le K_{n'}$ implies $S_{Q,n}\subseteq S_{Q,n'}$, and then $S_{Q,n'}$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_{Q,n}$ together with the constants from $A_{n'}$; the element $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ is the same in $\mathcal{F}$ for all $n$; and $\chi_{Q,n'}$ restricts to $\chi_{Q,n}$ on $S_{Q,n}$.
--
--   (7) For $Q,Q'\notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, if some place $P$ lies in $D_{Q,n}\cap D_{Q',n}$ for some $n$, then $Q=Q'$.
--
--   (8) For every $\tau$ in the subgroup of automorphisms of $\mathcal{F}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and arbitrary $\zeta'$, and for every proof $h_\tau$ that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$: the induced automorphism `R.resAut τ hτ` of the residue field acts on places preserving $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ in both directions, and for $Q\notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ one has `smulDisc τ (Dn Q n)` $=\{P:\tau^{-1}\cdot P\in D_{Q,n}\}=D_{\,\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q,\,n}$ for every $n$.
--
--   (9) For every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$, and every $n$ such that $\tau$ preserves $K_n$: for every $Q\notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, the coefficientwise action `arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')) τ` preserves $S_{Q,n}$ in both directions, and $\chi_{Q,n}$ is invariant under it.
--
--   (10) For every $g$ in the same subgroup generated by the level automorphisms, if the preimage of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{[1:0]}$ under $g$ differs from $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{[1:0]}$, then for all $Q,Q'\notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, all $n$ and all $P\in D_{Q,n}$ one has $g\cdot P\notin D_{Q',n}$.
--
--   (11) For $Q\notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, every $n$, every $P\in D_{Q,n}$ and every $s\in W$, it is not the case that both of the following hold: the image in $\mathcal{F}$ of the coefficientwise embedding of `jq` is integral at $P$ and, for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M')$, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that element minus $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$; and the same two conditions for the coefficientwise embedding of `qExpand ℚ M' jq` with `jNGeomGen κ M'` in place of `jGeomGen κ M'`.
--
--   (12) For every place $P$ of $\mathcal{F}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: if for every $s\in W$ it fails that (for all $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ integral wherever the coefficientwise image of `jq` is integral and with $R_0$-residue integral at $s$, and all $a\in A$ whose residue is $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ minus $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$), then there are $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $Q\notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $\cdot P\in D_{Q,n}$ for every $n$.
--
--   (13) There is a place $P$ of $\mathcal{F}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose valuation subring is `qIntegersBar (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (fieldBar q M')`, the ring of elements of non-negative Laurent order, together with a place $Q\notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ such that $P\in D_{Q,n}$ for every $n$.
--
--   This is the case $q=3$ of the construction, on the full-level modular curve of level $q^2M'$ over a valuation ring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $q$, of smooth-point charts along the Igusa branch: for each non-supersingular place $Q$ of the special fibre and each finite layer $K_n$ of constants, a local ring $S_{Q,n}$ with a formally smooth presentation $A_n[X]\to S_{Q,n}$, its residue disc $D_{Q,n}$ of places, and the equivariance of this data under the level automorphisms and under the inertia subgroup of $A$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaSmoothPointCharts_of_igusaGaussRing_allInertia_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaSmoothPointCharts_of_igusaGaussRing_allInertia_of_eq_three) in the analysis of the semistable reduction of modular curves at $q$ that underlies the level-lowering step.
